  "problem": "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables whose marginal density functions are as follows:\n\n$$\n{f}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}3{x}^{2}, & \\,0\\le x\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}4{y}^{3}, & \\,0\\le y\\le 1 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the joint probability density function $f(x,y).$\n\n*Hint: We do not know if $X$ and $Y$ are independent.*",
